---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MailtoCta from '../../components/MailtoCta.astro';
import { email, pageTitle, subjects } from '../../data/site';

const description =
  'Find repetitive coordination and information bottlenecks; decide honestly whether software, automation, or AI-assisted workflows are the right lever.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle('AI-assisted operational improvement')}
  description={description}
  currentPath="/services/ai-operations"
>
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <article class="prose-measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">Exploratory conversation. Friction first, models second.</p>
      <h1>AI-assisted operational improvement</h1>

      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Operators and small organisations stuck in repetitive coordination, manual handoffs, or tool
        sprawl.
      </p>

      <h2>Problem</h2>
      <p>
        “Add AI” without redesigning the work usually creates another dashboard. The target is
        friction, not model fashion.
      </p>

      <h2>What a discovery conversation covers</h2>
      <ol class="numbered-tight">
        <li>One named bottleneck you are willing to examine.</li>
        <li>A lightweight friction map (process vs software vs information stall).</li>
        <li>A leverage check: when automation or an agent surface helps, and when it does not.</li>
        <li>
          Engineering patterns we can show from products we ship (below), as building blocks, not
          your ROI.
        </li>
        <li>Data and secrets boundaries before any deeper access.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Engineering building blocks (from Trip and Move)</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <strong>MCP tools</strong> that call the same application actions as the UI. Agents cannot
          bypass tenancy or authorisation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Vision-assisted recognition</strong> for inventory contents with bring-your-own-key
          providers (Move).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hybrid search</strong>: full-text + trigram + vector embeddings (Move).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These show how we build agent-facing and AI-assisted software. They do not prove consulting
        delivery history or client outcomes.
      </p>
      <p>
        See <a href="/showroom">Trip and Move in the Showroom</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Example outputs (only if we continue under a separate agreement)</h2>
      <p>
        Friction map; prioritised interventions; an implemented workflow or application slice;
        operating notes.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p class="callout__label">Boundaries</p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>No invented ROI percentages or named client outcomes.</li>
          <li>A product demo is not your operational result.</li>
          <li>We do not replace regulated professional advice.</li>
          <li>We will not ask you to paste secrets into an unsolicited form.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Start a conversation</h2>
      <p>
        Email <strong>{email}</strong> with one repetitive bottleneck and your data-access
        constraints.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Subject suggestion: <span class="mono">{subjects.aiOps}</span></p>
      <p>We will say honestly if software or AI is the wrong lever.</p>
      <MailtoCta subject={subjects.aiOps} label={`Email ${email}`} />
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
